# Copy to .env — docker compose reads it automatically
FRONTEND_PORT=5173
BACKEND_PORT=3000
DB_PORT=5432

# Local LLM chat (Ollama on the host). `ollama list` shows what you have pulled;
# the model must support tool calling.
OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3.5:9b-q4_K_M
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434
# OLLAMA_TEMPERATURE=0.3
# Context window. Ollama silently drops the oldest messages past this, so raise
# it if answers start ignoring earlier tool results — at the cost of more VRAM.
# OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=65536
# OLLAMA_THINK=false
# CHAT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS=6
# How long Ollama holds the model in memory after you stop talking to it. A 9b
# at q4 with a 64k context is ~7GB for that whole window, and there is no state
# where the memory is freed but answers stay fast. The chat page pings while it
# is open, so this only covers walking away. "-1" pins it in memory for good.
# OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=5m
# When to load the model and prefill the system prompt and tool schemas:
#   page  load it when the chat page is opened — an idle app holds no memory
#   boot  also load it at startup, for a machine with memory to spare
#   off   no warm-up; the first question pays the load and the prefill
# OLLAMA_WARMUP=page

# Pull the last N seasons of stats into the cache at startup, in the background.
# Finished seasons never expire, so this is paid once for the life of a cache
# rather than once per restart, and a season already cached costs one DB read.
# "off" leaves the first question about an old season to pay for it.
# SPORTS_WARMUP=boot
# SPORTS_WARMUP_SEASONS=10
# Pause between season/group fetches. Nobody is waiting on this work, and a
# season of NFL stats is already eighteen weekly requests upstream.
# SPORTS_WARMUP_DELAY_MS=250

# Publish our own tools over MCP at /api/mcp for Claude Code, Claude Desktop and
# other agents. Generate with `openssl rand -hex 24`. Leave unset to keep the
# endpoint disabled.
# MCP_HTTP_TOKEN=

# MCP servers the chat can call, as JSON. Defaults to the bundled Sleeper server.
# MCP_SERVERS=[{"name":"sleeper","command":"node","args":["/app/node_modules/sleeper-mcp/dist/index.js"]}]
